{:edb/db-before-t 3692 :edb/db-after-t 3693 :edb/tx-data [[13194139537005 50 #inst "2026-10-18T03:05:29.920Z" 13194139537005 17592186576411 true] [17592186096523 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(80,60)$. So, our actual value is $y=60$.\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression curve that corresponds to $x=80$ has the $y$-coordinate $50$. So, our estimated value is\n\n$$\n\\widehat{y}=50\n$$\n\n![](images/49/49014ffe0943d7ce18084c359bc09ab0877cbc93a7d5df4beff83b0dadce47b7.png)\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nResidual &= Actual - Estimated \\\\\n&= y - \\widehat{y} \\\\\n&= 60 - 50 \\\\\n&= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $10$ animal species." 13194139537005 17592186576411 true] [17592186096523 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(80,60)$. So, our actual value is $y=60$.\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression curve that corresponds to $x=80$ has the $y$-coordinate $50$. So, our estimated value is\n\n$$\n\\widehat{y}=50\n$$\n\n![](images/49/49014ffe0943d7ce18084c359bc09ab0877cbc93a7d5df4beff83b0dadce47b7.png)\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nResidual &= Actual - Estimated \\\\\n&= y - y^(^) \\\\\n&= 60 - 50 \\\\\n&= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $10$ animal species." 13194139537005 17592186576411 false] [17592186110954 1071 "![](images/bd/bd99171c2696038851bf0fdf7297d2e4a60791f6b11083af8cd51baf48930b2d.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of $\\overset{^}{COE}?$" 13194139537005 17592186576411 false] [17592186110954 1071 "![](images/bd/bd99171c2696038851bf0fd